# A list concatenated with a non-list via `+`. CPython raises TypeError at RUN
# time; this used to silently corrupt the result (reinterpreting the list
# pointer as string data) — bug-nilpy-list-plus-nonlist-silently-corrupts-
# instead-of-typeerror.
#
# It was then made a COMPILE error, which was loud but still diverged from
# CPython: a `try/except TypeError` around it could not build. As of
# bug-nilpy-missing-arith-dunder-aborts-compile-instead-of-raising it is a
# genuine runtime TypeError, so the file COMPILES and raises when run — which
# is what this test now asserts, together with the handler actually running.
a = [1, 2, 3]
try:
    print(a + "x")
except TypeError:
    print("caught list+str")
print("still running")
